# A Luxel library scene — Apache-2.0. Grammar: library/README.md.
# Snowfall with no engine: `snowfall-tile` is a 16x16 LOOP TILE whose 16 frames
# move its flakes down one pixel each (and wrap), so `fit tile` over the whole
# panel is a seamless snowfall that costs no pattern layer. The one engine is
# the drift-mode Starfield, ramped to an indigo night. Designed at 32x32
# (`U`): the greeting and the trees zoom with the panel — a second, smaller
# tree further off, its lights stepping at a different rate — while the snow
# is pinned to panel pixels (`X abs`), so a bigger panel gets more flakes,
# not bigger ones.
S - Silent Night
U 32 32
L pat 0 0 0 0 normal 100 none fill 1
N Sky
I @pat/starfield-2d
C sliderMode 65536
R 100 0:03041a 120:1a2350 255:dfe6ff
L sprite 19 15 12 13 normal 100 none fill 3
N Tree 2
I @spr/christmas-tree
A 3
L sprite 1 6 0 0 normal 100 none fill 1
N Tree
I @spr/christmas-tree
L sprite 0 0 0 0 normal 100 none tile 1
N Snow
I @spr/snowfall-tile
X abs
L text 0 0 0 0 normal 100 black fill 1
N Greeting
T lit MERRY CHRISTMAS
F tiny ffd166 l left 12
